q q .423529 .478431 .501961 rg BT/F4+0 8 Tf 59.53 46.8 TD (August 2026)Tj ET .137255 .156863 .172549 rg BT/F2+0 8.5 Tf 547.574 46.8 TD (7)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 59.53 711 cm .078431 .094118 .105882 rg BT/F3+0 11 Tf 0 2 TD (2.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 59.53 685.5 cm .062745 .078431 .090196 rg BT/F2+0 20.5 Tf 0 4 TD (Why This Reckoning Is Structurally Unavoidable)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 59.53 676.8 cm .866667 .890196 .894118 RG 1 J .7 w n 0 0 m 492.94 0 l S Q q 1 0 0 1 59.53 644.7 cm .078431 .094118 .105882 rg BT/F2+0 11.6 Tf 0 2.9 TD (The two curves running in opposite directions)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 59.53 545.8 cm .137255 .156863 .172549 rg BT/F4+0 10 Tf 0 81.2 TD (The most confusing part of the current moment, for enterprise finance teams, is that two opposing trends)Tj 0 -15.199997 TD (are running at the same time. Per-token inference prices have fallen sharply, by roughly nine-fold to)Tj 0 -15.200001 TD (nine-hundred-fold per year across various capability benchmarks tracked by Epoch AI, and Gartner)Tj T* (forecasts a further ninety percent reduction by 2030. At the same time, total enterprise AI bills are rising)Tj T* (rapidly. Both can be true, because token prices and total token consumption are not the same thing. Costs)Tj 0 -15.2 TD (per unit are collapsing. Units consumed are exploding. The product of the two is what shows up on the bill.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 59.53 277.2837 cm .290196 .333333 .352941 rg BT/F5+0 8.3 Tf 0 26.2 TD (Figure 2.)Tj .411765 .462745 .486275 rg/F6+0 8.3 Tf ( Two curves running in opposite directions. Per-token API prices for GPT-4-class capability fell roughly 75-fold between)Tj 0 -11.5 TD (2023 and 2026, while average enterprise annual AI bills rose nearly 18-fold over the same period. Sources: Zylos Research;)Tj T* (AnalyticsWeek; Oplexa; Epoch AI.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 59.53 189.2837 cm .137255 .156863 .172549 rg BT/F4+0 10 Tf 0 66 TD (This pattern is not new. The same dynamic played out in cloud computing a decade ago: per-instance)Tj 0 -15.200001 TD (prices fell consistently, while total cloud bills grew steadily, because consumption grew faster than unit)Tj T* (prices fell. That pattern produced an entire industry, cloud FinOps, whose job is to discipline consumption)Tj T* (against business value. AI is on the same trajectory, only steeper, because the consumption multiplier from)Tj 0 -15.2 TD (agentic workflows is structurally larger than anything cloud computing produced.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 59.53 157.1837 cm .078431 .094118 .105882 rg BT/F2+0 11.6 Tf 0 2.9 TD (Why end users cannot solve this themselves at scale)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 59.53 73.48371 cm .137255 .156863 .172549 rg BT/F4+0 10 Tf 0 66 TD (When a new cost category appears, enterprises usually follow a predictable pattern: first they ignore it,)Tj 0 -15.200001 TD (then they try to manage it through procurement, then they try to build internal capability to address it)Tj T* (directly. AI is now in the early stages of the second phase, and a meaningful number of enterprises are)Tj T* (starting to consider the third: building internal AI infrastructure, training their own models, running)Tj 0 -15.2 TD (inference on their own GPUs.)Tj ET Q Q /fzFrm0 Do
