y, in which case the intermediary tier this paper describes would not)Tj 0 -15.200001 TD (form as a distinct procurement category but would be absorbed upward. The incentive argument suggests)Tj T* (they will not, because every saved token is revenue they do not capture. But incentive arguments hold in)Tj T* (aggregate, not in every case. A foundation lab that decides enterprise margin matters more than total)Tj 0 -15.2 TD (token volume could change the structure materially.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 59.53 294.5 cm .137255 .156863 .172549 rg BT/F2+0 10 Tf 0 96.4 TD (Enterprises could absorb higher AI costs as a new normal.)Tj/F4+0 10 Tf ( The paper argues that financial discipline will)Tj 0 -15.199997 TD (arrive when boards begin demanding measurable return on AI spend. That arrival depends on)Tj T* (macroeconomic conditions, on competitive dynamics within each sector, and on whether the productivity)Tj 0 -15.200001 TD (gains AI delivers prove durable enough to justify open-ended spending. If AI productivity gains are large)Tj T* (enough and visible enough, enterprises may simply accept higher AI bills the way they accept higher cloud)Tj T* (bills: as a cost of doing modern business. The forced choice this paper describes may not arrive on the)Tj 0 -15.2 TD (timeline implied.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 59.53 118.2 cm .137255 .156863 .172549 rg BT/F4+0 10 Tf 0 157.2 TD (The thesis is most likely to hold under three conditions, expressed here as approximate thresholds rather)Tj -.003333 Tw 0 -15.199997 TD (than precise predictions. First: agentic and multi-step workflows continue to grow as a share of production)Tj 0 Tw T* (AI spend, plausibly reaching 30 percent or more by end-2027, consistent with current adoption)Tj T* (trajectories and Gartner's 5x to 30x token multiplier estimate for agentic models. Second: foundation lab)Tj T* (per-token prices decline by less than roughly 5x annually through 2028, meaning unit-cost reductions do)Tj T* (not outrun the consumption multiplier; this is consistent with publicly reported lab financials showing)Tj T* (losses substantially exceeding revenue even as revenue grows. Third: CFO scrutiny of AI spending)Tj 0 -15.200001 TD (continues to intensify along the trajectory the FinOps adoption data already shows, the 31 percent to 63)Tj T* (percent rise from 2024 to 2025, such that AI cost governance becomes standard practice across most)Tj T* (large enterprises by 2028. The thesis weakens materially if any one of these three conditions reverses.)Tj 0 -15.2 TD (Readers should weigh the argument against their own view of how likely each condition is to hold.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 59.53 78.7 cm .137255 .156863 .172549 rg BT/F4+0 10 Tf 0 20.4 TD (These thresholds are illustrative, derived from current analyst trajectories and reported lab financials)Tj 0 -15.2 TD (rather than from formal econometric modeling. They are intended as defensible reference points against)Tj ET Q Q
