termediaries who)Tj T* (specialize in it. They will operate with the highest output value per token and the lowest exposure to)Tj T* (foundation pricing volatility. They will produce comparable or better business outcomes for a fraction of)Tj 0 -15.2 TD (the cost, and that cost-and-exposure gap will compound as AI volumes grow.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 59.53 316.3 cm .137255 .156863 .172549 rg BT/F4+0 10 Tf 0 66 TD (Most enterprises are not in a position to build that combined discipline \(engineering depth, validation)Tj 0 -15.200001 TD (pipelines, domain-aware structured logic, and continuous token economics\) on their own. A procurement)Tj T* (pattern that aligns incentives more tightly, the one this paper has proposed naming Deterministic AI)Tj T* (Infrastructure, is beginning to appear, in advance of the demand wave that will require it. The window for)Tj 0 -15.2 TD (foresight is open. It will not stay open indefinitely.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 59.53 185.6 cm .137255 .156863 .172549 rg BT/F4+0 10 Tf 0 111.6 TD (Two predictions, offered for readers to test against future data. If agentic and multi-step workflows reach)Tj 0 -15.199997 TD (roughly 40 percent of enterprise AI spend by end-2027, and foundation-model lab losses remain above 30)Tj T* (percent of revenue through that period, then adoption of DAII-style procurement among large enterprises)Tj T* (should exceed 25 percent by end-2027 and become standard procurement language by 2029. If those)Tj 0 -15.200001 TD (two preconditions fail to materialize, if agentic share stalls or foundation-lab economics resolve toward)Tj T* (sustainable margin more quickly than current losses suggest, then the procurement pattern described)Tj T* (here may emerge more slowly, or in a different form than this paper anticipates. The thesis is offered as)Tj 0 -15.2 TD (falsifiable on those terms.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 59.53 82.5 cm .047059 .066667 .07451 rg n 0 0 492.94 86 re f* 1 1 1 rg BT/F2+0 13.2 Tf 41.9888 46.704 TD <024149206973206e6f74206